ss.yaml` includes that setup logic.","locale":"en"},"98":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-96","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#1-enable-dataload-in-cacheruntimeclass","content":"Fluid injects these environment variables into the DataLoad job:","locale":"en"},"99":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-97","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#1-enable-dataload-in-cacheruntimeclass","content":"| Variable                  | Meaning                            |\n| ------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `FLUID_DATALOAD_METADATA` | Whether metadata should be loaded. |","locale":"en","table":"table-4"},"100":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-98","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#1-enable-dataload-in-cacheruntimeclass","content":"| Variable                   | Meaning                       |\n| -------------------------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `FLUID_DATALOAD_DATA_PATH` | Paths to load, joined by `:`. |","locale":"en","table":"table-4"},"101":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-99","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#1-enable-dataload-in-cacheruntimeclass","content":"| Variable                       | Meaning                                     |\n| ------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------- |\n| `FLUID_DATALOAD_PATH_REPLICAS` | Replica count for each path, joined by `:`. |","locale":"en","table":"table-4"},"102":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-100","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#1-enable-dataload-in-cacheruntimeclass","content":"The Curvine CacheRuntimeClass sample uses an inline DataLoad script because Fluid runs data operations as short-lived Jobs. The script first generates Curvine config from the Fluid runtime JSON. If that file is not mounted, it falls back to Dataset metadata, pod labels, and finally a DataLoad name pattern such as `<dataset>-load`.","locale":"en"},"103":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-101","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#1-enable-dataload-in-cacheruntimeclass","content":"When Fluid passes a Dataset path such as `/minio`, the script checks Curvine mount metadata and resolves it to the real Curvine load source before running `cv load --watch`. This keeps DataLoad aligned with `mountUFS`.","locale":"en"},"104":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-102","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#2-create-a-dataload-resource","content":"Example:","locale":"en"},"105":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-103","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#2-create-a-dataload-resource","content":"Apply it:","locale":"en"},"106":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-104","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#2-create-a-dataload-resource","content":"`spec.dataset` selects the Dataset. `spec.target[].path` selects the Dataset path to preload. Fluid passes the target paths to the job through `FLUID_DATALOAD_DATA_PATH`.","locale":"en"},"107":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration-105","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/fluid-integration#3-check-the-dataload-job","content":"The DataLoad job is successful only if the Curvine load command exits successfully for every target path. If `cv load --watc