file-read#5-test-conclusion","content":"Far beyond native storage: Curvine's optimal read performance reached 6174 images/second, which is 3.68 times that of native MinIO at 1675 images/second. The basic version reached 5615 images/second, which is already 3.35 times that of native MinIO.","locale":"en"},"581":{"id":"/docs/Benchmark/small-file-read-34","page_id":"/docs/Benchmark/small-file-read","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Benchmark/small-file-read#5-test-conclusion","content":"Significant metadata cache gains: after metadata cache was enabled, performance improved by 6.8% to 10.0% compared with the Curvine basic version, and the client metadata cache delivered the best optimization effect.","locale":"en"},"582":{"id":"/docs/Benchmark/small-file-read-35","page_id":"/docs/Benchmark/small-file-read","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Benchmark/small-file-read#5-test-conclusion","content":"Efficient metadata mechanism: the native Curvine basic version already achieved high-performance reads of 5615 images/second. It can meet AI small-file read requirements without relying on cache, reducing configuration complexity and O&M costs.","locale":"en"},"583":{"id":"/docs/Benchmark/small-file-read-36","page_id":"/docs/Benchmark/small-file-read","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Benchmark/small-file-read#5-test-conclusion","content":"Strong mode compatibility: both `fs-mode` and `cache-mode` can stably deliver high performance, adapting to storage requirements in different business scenarios while balancing performance and flexibility.","locale":"en"},"584":{"id":"/docs/Contribute/benchmark-guide","page_id":"/docs/Contribute/benchmark-guide","type":"page","content":"Benchmark Guide","breadcrumbs":["Documents","Contributor Guide"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/Contribute/benchmark-guide","locale":"en"},"585":{"id":"/docs/Contribute/benchmark-guide-0","page_id":"/docs/Contribute/benchmark-guide","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Contribute/benchmark-guide#before-you-