rnetes-quick-start-8","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start","content":"This guide runs Curvine on a local Kubernetes cluster with the Helm charts, then mounts a Curvine volume in a pod through the CSI driver. It takes you from an empty machine to a pod that writes a file to Curvine and reads it back.","locale":"en"},"1869":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start-9","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start","content":"It uses kind. A minikube variant is at the end. The two Helm charts are:","locale":"en"},"1870":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start-10","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start","content":"| Chart             | Release   | Namespace | Purpose                   |\n| ----------------- | --------- | --------- | ------------------------- |\n| `curvine/curvine` | `curvine` | `curvine` | Curvine master and worker |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"1871":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start-11","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start","content":"| Chart                 | Release       | Namespace        | Purpose                                           |\n| --------------------- | ------------- | ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `curvine/curvine-csi` | `curvine-csi` | `curvine-system` | CSI driver that mounts Curvine into pods via FUSE |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"1872":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start-12","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start","content":"For production clusters and the full list of chart values, see Kubernetes Deployment and K8S CSI Driver.","locale":"en"},"1873":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-