ss method.** The Curvine cluster (Master + Worker) must be running first. FUSE is only needed when applications require a POSIX mount point. See Deployment Architecture for the role of each component.","locale":"en"},"2144":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse-11","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse#prerequisites","content":"**Curvine cluster** is running (Master and Worker started). See Bare Metal Deployment or Quick Start.","locale":"en"},"2145":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse-12","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse#prerequisites","content":"**Configuration**: The node where FUSE runs must have access to the cluster config (e.g. `conf/curvine-cluster.toml`) and correct Master address.","locale":"en"},"2146":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse-13","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse#prerequisites","content":"**Supported systems**: FUSE 2 and FUSE 3 are supported; behavior may vary by distribution. See Supported Linux Distributions.","locale":"en"},"2147":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse-14","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse#start-fuse","content":"Run from the installation directory (e.g. `build/dist` or the extracted release package):","locale":"en"},"2148":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse-15","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse#start-fuse","content":"**Default mount path**: `/curvine-fuse`","locale":"en"},"2149":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse-16","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse#start-fuse","content":"**Default config**: `conf/curvine-cluster.toml` (relative to current working directory when the process starts)","locale":"en"},"2150":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse-17","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse#start-fuse","content":"Use `bin/curvine-fuse.sh stop` to stop, or `bin/curvine-fuse.sh restart` to restart.","locale":"en"},"2151":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse-18","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse#use-the-mount-point","content":"Under the FUSE mount path you can use standard Linux file commands: `ls`, `cat`, `rm`, `mv`, `mkdir`, `du`, `cp`, etc.","locale":"en"},"2152":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse-19","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse#use-the-mount-point","content":"Example:","locale":"en"},"2153":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse-20","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse#use-the-mount-point","content":"Data written here is stored in the Curvine cluster; you can also access paths that correspond to mounted UFS (unified file system view).","locale":"en"},"2154":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse-21","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse#optional-parameters","content":"When starting FUSE, you can pass through options to the underlying `curvine-fuse` binary, for example:","locale":"en"},"2155":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse-22","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse#optional-parameters","content":"| Option       | Description      | Default         |\n| ------------ | ---------------- | --------------- |\n| `--mnt-path` | Mount point path | `/curvine-fuse` |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"2156":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse-23","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse#optional-parameters","content":"| Option          | Description              | Default                     |\n| --------------- | ------------------------ | --------------------------- |\n| `-c` / `--conf` | Cluster config file path | `conf/curvine-cluster.toml` |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"2157":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse-24","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse#optional-parameters","content":"| Option      | Description                                 | Default |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------------- | ------- |\n| `--fs-path` | Root path inside Curvine to expose at mount | `/`     |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"2158":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse-25","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse#optional-parameters","content":"| Option         | Description      | Default      |\n| -------------- | ---------------- | ------------ |\n| `--io-threads` | I/O thread count | config value |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"2159":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse-26","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse#optional-parameters","content":"| Option             | Description         | Default      |\n| ------------------ | ------------------- | ------------ |\n| `--worker-threads` | Worker thread count | config value |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"2160":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse-27","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse#optional-parameters","content":"Run `bin/curvine-fuse.sh --help` (or `lib/curvine-fuse --help` under the installation directory) to list all options.","locale":"en"},"2161":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse-28","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse#check-configuration-without-mounting","content":"`curvine-fuse` exposes two helper subcommands that are useful in CI and before a\nrolling mount change:","locale":"en"},"2162":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse-29","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse#check-configuration-without-mounting","content":"`validate-config` loads the config, verifies that `fuse.state_dir` is writable\n(creating it when missing), and warns about unrecognized `[fuse]` keys — the\nkind of typo that would otherwise silently keep a default. It exits non-zero\nwhen the config cannot be parsed or the state directory is unusable. It does not\nmount, and it does not check Master reachability. The Curvine CSI driver calls it\nduring node-side mount setup.","locale":"en"},"2163":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse-30","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse#fuse-support-level","content":"Curvine FUSE supports:","locale":"en"},"2164":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse-31","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse#fuse-support-level","content":"Standard file read/write and directory operations","locale":"en"},"2165":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse-32","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse#fuse-support-level","content":"User/group and permission semantics","locale":"en"},"2166":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse-33","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse#fuse-support-level","content":"Extended attributes (xattr), symbolic links (symlink), hard links (link)","locale":"en"},"2167":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse-34","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse#fuse-support-level","content":"FUSE driver behavior can